[2026-11-02 19:53:05 ET] Timeline (seconds from the owner pressing enter; D = the script sees the bridge down, at most 5 s after):
  T+0            owner stops the bridge (the switch loses its controller; workload frames start to be dropped)
  D              no_controller_before_probe: 12 s of 2,000 pps (sampler lead-in 1.5 s, so about 16 s with the ssh calls)
  D+~18          probe starts on the Jetson (must start by D+25 or it is not started); it binds 6633 and waits up to 35 s for the switch
  P+r            the switch connects (r unmeasured), the probe reads the table (read 1)
  P+r            probe_connected: 12 s of the same traffic while the probe holds the session
  P+r+20         read 2; the probe exits and the switch has no controller again
  T+110          the detached timer armed by the owner's command starts the bridge (the probe is dead by D+97 at the latest, the CLI's own limits)
  +6 s          bridge answering again; 10 s settle; isolation status read; after_bridge_back: 12 s of the same traffic
Probe limits: overall 65 s, reconnect wait 35 s, readback timeout 8 s, 2 readbacks 20 s apart; remote last-resort kill at 72 s.
Worst-case blackout: 110 s sleep + about 6 s restart = about 116 s, under the isolation watcher's alert of 150 s (3 polls of 60 s); the sleep is fixed, so the blackout is about that long whether or not the probe finishes early.
Owner command (one line, on the Jetson): sudo sh -c 'systemd-run --unit=away-restart-$(date +%s) --on-active=110s systemctl start zodiac-bridge && systemctl stop zodiac-bridge'
To end the outage early: sudo systemctl stop 'away-restart-*.timer'; sudo systemctl start zodiac-bridge
